1.	Prepare test cases – Create different situations to check each feature.
	2.	Test individual components – Check each module separately.
	3.	Integration testing – Check whether different modules work correctly together.
	4.	Functional testing – Verify that all required features work as expected.
	5.	User interface testing – Check buttons, forms, navigation, layout, and usability.
	6.	Performance testing – Check the speed, stability, and response of the system.
	7.	Find and fix bugs – Identify errors and correct them.
	8.	Final testing – Test the complete system before deployment.
